WEBVTT

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:04.040
There's always a blue sky in your heart

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.530
Good weather again today.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.440
Luna! It's mornin'!

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.110
Yeesh.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:37.620
How long ya gonna sleep?

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:40.020
Today's the day we're goin' to the Eastern Woods, ain't it?

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:41.560
Luna?

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:47.310
Oh no! A bad fever!

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:49.980
How many degrees?

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:52.880
39.1ﾂｰC.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.060
That's high!

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:56.390
Luna...

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:00.120
Did something happen?

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.330
It's bad news--Luna has a fever!

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:08.730
Luna... are you okay?

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:17.670
Don't! Just go to sleep!

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:22.230
--You have a fever!
--I have to go...

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:24.870
Don't! Just sleep peacefully for today!

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:34.840
A cold?

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.000
Chako's checking into it right now.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.630
Maybe she's just worn out.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.880
Then I guess we'll have to delay the trip.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:46.340
I guess we'll get to take our first day off in a while.

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:48.040
Don't speak so cheerfully!

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.160
Aren't you worried about Luna?

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:53.280
It's not like worrying about her will make her better.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.660
Stop it! We have to be quiet.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.490
I can't tell with just my abilities.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.390
Oh no! Her fever's gone up again!

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:17.580
How was it?

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:20.950
I ain't sure of the cause.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:25.040
If we can't do somethin' to bring the fever down, it'll be painful.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:28.090
It would be good if we had some medicinal herbs to help her fever, but...

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.310
Accordin' to my data, Kudzu roots are effective at lowerin' fever.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:33.360
Kudzu roots?

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:37.000
It's a leguminous plant species that grows wrapped 'round trees.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.340
The key ingredient's in the root.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:40.900
I see.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:42.460
And that will bring it down?

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:46.060
I got the image data, so I'll search for that.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:46.900
Very well.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:49.900
Bell, do you know of anything else?

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.590
When we didn't have medicine, I've boiled and drank Mugwort.

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:56.930
It's got various vitamins...

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:58.900
...and it seems to be effective in bringing' down fever too.

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:02.200
It's not enough alone, but for Luna it should be fine.

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.860
But we've never seen Mugwort.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:07.530
It's okay. I'll search for the Mugwort.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:09.180
I'll help too!

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:12.140
And I want some nutritious food.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.650
Like fruit or eggs.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:16.860
I'll get the eggs.

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:18.250
No helping it.

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.140
I'll go search for fruit.

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:24.040
Then, we'll leave Sharla to attend the patient...

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:25.920
...and split up to search.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:26.860
Wait!

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:32.650
I want to search with Chako!

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:35.260
Are you sure?

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:39.180
You might get attacked by a giant lizard or a man-eating plant.

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:40.090
But...

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:43.110
...I'm the one who knows best where plants can be found.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.420
There might be dangerous cliffs or something too.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.630
Can a weakling like you really do it?

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.480
I want to be of some use to Luna!

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:55.730
Very well.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:58.230
I'll attend to Luna.

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:00.010
Sharla, please go with Chako.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.130
Thank you, Menori.

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:41.180
Now I'm soaking wet.

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:03.760
What d'we do? It's a penetratin' rain.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:04.830
Let's go.

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:08.740
"Let's go?" We'll get soakin' wet. Is that okay?

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:10.450
It's fine.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:14.800
H-hey, wait!

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:17.160
Sharla, I'm in trouble if you leave!

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:25.840
Rain...

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:29.240
Yes. If we'd left today, we would have been rained on.

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:30.980
Good thing we delayed it.

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:32.780
Where's Sharla?

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:35.090
She went to search for herbs.

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:40.240
It's the first time I've seen Sharla like that.

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:45.120
She desperately wanted to help you.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:51.510
It's good to have friends.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:05.840
Be careful you don't slip.

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:13.340
Sharla!

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:15.440
You okay?

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:21.570
Ow!

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:25.560
You can't go any further.

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:32.050
Sorry, Luna. Maybe I should just sit out.

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:37.510
If you sit out now, they get what they wanted. I definitely don't want to lose.

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:39.180
It's okay.

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:41.220
I'm with you.

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:43.810
Although I may be a little unreliable.

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:49.960
Sharla, you understand best of all that Bell is really a kind person.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.300
Sharla, let's give our best!

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:55.090
I'm okay.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.850
As long as I'm walking, it won't hurt.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:05.430
You ain't okay at all!

00:09:06.490 --> 00:09:08.160
I can't give up just from this.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:10.490
Luna taught me that!

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:13.980
Okay! I'll help too!

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:21.340
Hey, Chako...

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:24.870
How did Luna get so strong?

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.290
Let's see...

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:30.210
It might look that way from where you stand, Sharla...

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:33.030
...but she ain't really that strong.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:36.140
The first time I met her...

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:38.500
...Luna was a total coward.

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:43.040
This was about, oh, eight years back.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:46.840
Back then, Luna's mother dyin' was still fresh in her mind.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.440
...and she always cried.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:10:00.040
Welcome home, Luna. There's a snack for you in the fridge.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:02.610
I'm home!

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:04.300
Luna?

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:05.800
Are you here?

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:07.900
Found you.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.420
Back here again?

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:11.440
Luna, you like this place.

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:27.740
Ta-da!

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:33.080
I'm always away from home because of work...

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:35.390
...I thought you'd be lonely by yourself.

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:37.840
Luna, this is your new friend.

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:41.200
Hello!

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:43.490
I don't need it!

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:49.410
Luna! Hey!

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:56.500
I was already hated by Luna...

00:10:57.040 --> 00:11:00.270
...but her dad said we'd be able to patch things up 'n chased after her.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:05.630
But Luna wouldn't open her heart up to me.

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:20.460
I left Luna's house, but I didn't have a destination.

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:24.160
In an observation park where you could see the real stars...

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:27.570
...I ended up lookin' up at the stars before I even realized.

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:29.780
What are you doing?

00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:33.660
I ain't doin' nothin'!

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:39.590
And why're you in a place like this?

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:48.870
Whenever I get lonely, I come here and look up at the stars.

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:50.520
Really?

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:55.840
Lookin' up at the starry sky kinda calms your feelings, right?

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:58.640
Are you lonely too?

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:00.440
Darn right I am!

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:04.680
There ain't a robot pet who wouldn't be lonely if her master hated her.

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:06.570
I'm sorry.

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:09.330
It's okay.

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:14.880
I'm Luna!

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:17.110
I...

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:19.170
...hate my old name.

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:23.520
I was thrown away by my old master.

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:40.970
"Minna no Ie" means Everyone's House.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:49.000
I was thrown away by my old master.

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:53.240
I don't really know why...

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:58.230
...but I was worn-out, my main switch was turned off, and I was thrown away.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:00.740
I was put on a conveyor belt...

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:03.870
...and was gonna be disposed of with the rest of the scrap.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:12.530
When I was about to be melted down, right in the nick of time, your dad found me and pulled me out.

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:17.430
And then he washed me and fixed me up good as new.

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:20.160
And he put me in a box as a present.

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:23.090
So that's what happened.

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:26.290
Yeah, so I hate my old name.

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:29.070
You're a girl?

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:30.120
Sure am!

00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:34.060
Will you give me a new, elegant name?

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:35.800
Let's see...

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:38.220
Cha... Chako!

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.500
What's elegant about that?

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:42.890
It's cute!

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:45.140
No, no. Make it a different one!

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:58.620
Can't help it! I'll just have to put up with that name!

00:13:58.980 --> 00:13:59.690
Really?

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:02.890
Nice to meet you, Chako!

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:08.560
Nice to meet you, too.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:20.990
Since then, Luna 'n I became friends that never doubt what's in each others' hearts.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:24.190
But then, two years after that...

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:26.890
...her dad died...

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:33.680
All girls, whoever they are, have glass slippers in their heart.

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:35.200
Glass slippers?

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:38.030
A dream they had when they were little...

00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:39.700
...or some fantasy.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:45.550
When Luna was eight, her glass slippers broke.

00:14:46.230 --> 00:14:48.440
Mine did when I was thrown away.

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:52.540
Since then, Luna 'n I have lived together, just the two of us.

00:14:53.730 --> 00:14:55.470
So that's what happened.

00:14:56.010 --> 00:15:00.210
It's a sad story that brings tears to those who hear it and those who tell it.

00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:03.660
But I wonder why...

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:10.130
Even though so many sad things have happened to her, Luna's always bright and cheerful.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.920
When times are tough, look up to the sky.

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:17.910
There may be rainy days, but there's  always a blue sky in your heart.

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:22.510
Whether it's a pitch-dark night or a day with bad weather,

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:25.170
so long's the sun's still there, a day with a blue sky will come.

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:27.460
There's always a blue sky in your heart.

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:28.360
Exactly.

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:30.850
So you can't worry about things forever.

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:32.670
There's a blue sky in your heart.

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:44.890
Good.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:50.610
There's lots of them!

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:55.190
If you crumble the Mugwort leaves and rub them in a wound, they'll also act as an antiseptic.

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:58.110
So, I think this much should be enough.

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:06.980
It looks like a dead end.

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:13.170
They're beautiful flowers.

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:17.560
Sharla, these plants look a bunch like the ones in my data!

00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:20.290
We'll know once we dig out the roots, right?

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:24.400
That's true, but the roots are on the cliff side.

00:16:26.430 --> 00:16:27.930
Chako, a little more!

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:33.210
I can't, I'm at my limit!

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:46.150
Sharla, hang on!

00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:50.590
We made it up.

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:52.090
Are you hurt?

00:17:01.170 --> 00:17:02.890
This is it! No mistake!

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:13.340
This is medicine.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:17.560
It might taste bad, but put up with it 'n drink it all.

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:36.740
Hey, Chako...

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:41.280
Today, you talked about glass slippers, right?

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:48.190
Even though I'm fourteen years old, I still have glass slippers in my heart.

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:54.210
Even now I cling tightly to my glass slippers and keep dreaming.

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:56.520
It's not like it's a bad thing.

00:17:57.190 --> 00:17:58.640
Luna told me the same thing.

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:03.340
But because of that, I don't think I've been able to accept reality yet.

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:08.460
You see, I love fantasy stories.

00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:10.980
I've even written some myself.

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:12.910
But...

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:20.350
The princess stealthily snuck out of the castle and went to play in the forest.

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:26.860
In the forest, many beautiful flowers were blooming, and many cute animals gathered.

00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:29.560
What'cha writin'?

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:30.790
What are you doing?

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:32.390
Lemme look for a sec!

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:33.330
Stop it!

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:35.290
Give that back!

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:38.070
Give it back!

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:42.810
What, what? "Once upon a time, there was a docile princess."

00:18:42.910 --> 00:18:46.900
"She failed at everything she tried, and was only good at giving names to things."

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:48.850
Ha! That sounds like you!

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:52.620
Please, give it back!

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:59.010
Once, I reached out to a girl in the class who was being left out and became friends with her.

00:19:01.190 --> 00:19:04.830
But because of that, I was left out as well.

00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:10.810
I'd always been bad at being part of a group, so it didn't really bother me...

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:16.510
...all of a sudden, the girl I reached out to had switched to the side of those leaving me out.

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:23.130
After that, no matter how I tried to make friends, I could never take even one step forward.

00:19:24.340 --> 00:19:27.460
I retreated into my shell more and more.

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:33.140
I felt that if I didn't, my glass slippers that were so precious to me might be broken.

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:38.580
I thought that one day, my own wonderful story would start.

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:41.880
A tale like one of those fantasy stories.

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:46.510
Just then, Luna appeared before me.

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:50.240
Even though I'd just met her, for some reason I warmed up to Luna.

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:53.480
Because nothing like that had happened to me before.

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:57.290
I'm sure it's because Luna was so kind and cheerful.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:02.520
Since then, the story I'd been imagining really began.

00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:08.820
But now that it's begun, I see that there's more to reality than just happy times.

00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:12.010
There are many hard or frightening times...

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:15.930
...and the heroes of the story can't be disheartened.

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:19.900
But I became disheartened right away, and became a burden to everyone.

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:23.780
That's not true.

00:20:28.230 --> 00:20:30.180
Luna, you were awake!

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:34.730
Sharla, you've worked very hard since we came to this island.

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:40.240
The best at braiding rope and cooking food is you, Sharla.

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:44.540
And when we come back to Everyone's House,

00:20:44.550 --> 00:20:48.010
it makes us feel relieved when you say, "Welcome home," to us.

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:50.580
Like we've really come home.

00:20:51.490 --> 00:20:52.110
Luna...

00:20:53.760 --> 00:20:56.540
Sharla, you're not being a burden on anybody.

00:20:57.510 --> 00:20:58.320
Thank you.

00:20:59.050 --> 00:20:59.760
I...

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:01.540
I guess I...

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:03.600
have been running away from reality until now,

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:06.610
but from now on I'll try to accept reality, a little at a time.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:10.580
Reality's not that bad all the time, after all.

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:13.790
The reason I've made so many friends...

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:15.890
...is because I came to this planet.

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:17.440
Sharla...

00:21:22.430 --> 00:21:23.990
Your fever's mostly gone down.

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:25.260
What a relief!

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:30.290
If I'm going to be attended to courteously...

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:32.690
...maybe I should stay sick a little longer.

00:21:32.690 --> 00:21:36.080
What'cha sayin'? I should punish you for that!

00:21:36.490 --> 00:21:37.210
That's right!

00:21:39.490 --> 00:21:40.710
Sorry, sorry!

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:42.570
You seem to have gotten better.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:43.990
Menori!

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:46.770
Thanks to all of you.

00:21:47.520 --> 00:21:48.340
Thank you!

00:21:51.890 --> 00:21:53.610
It'll be dawn soon.

00:21:54.810 --> 00:21:56.730
I want to see a bit of the sunrise.

00:21:57.230 --> 00:21:59.050
Sure, let's take a look.

00:22:17.730 --> 00:22:19.020
Good morning, Luna.

00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:20.740
Are you okay now?

00:22:22.210 --> 00:22:23.950
Your skin tone looks better too.

00:22:24.510 --> 00:22:25.320
Thanks.

00:22:33.100 --> 00:22:34.940
The sun has risen again.

00:22:35.260 --> 00:22:37.860
And so, there'll always be a blue sky in your heart.

00:22:38.140 --> 00:22:38.950
That's right!

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:40.280
What's that?

00:22:41.130 --> 00:22:42.440
It's Chako's pet phrase.

00:22:42.890 --> 00:22:45.870
She's been saying that since I was little.

00:22:46.170 --> 00:22:48.310
But Sharla, why do you know it?

00:22:49.830 --> 00:22:51.190
What's it matter?

00:22:51.590 --> 00:22:53.910
Looks like there'll be good weather today!

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:08.990
We delayed our trip to the Eastern Woods until Luna recovered...

00:23:09.630 --> 00:23:13.240
Shingo couldn't wait to see the advanced civilization...

00:23:13.530 --> 00:23:16.830
...and he tempted Howard and Chako to go with him!

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:21.550
Luna can't seem to hear the mysterious voice, so we get lost in the forest.

00:23:22.190 --> 00:23:23.950
Which way should we go?

00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:28.000
Next time: These are the Eastern Woods!?
